  "body": "Follow-up of PR #3353 (#3316), from the report of its worker. The readings are from that worker's runs on head 9939a6238.\n\nWith \"Pass starts at: Outside\" on the fig8 2D Offset, the plan cuts each level as open pieces. A piece that cannot join the piece before it through material that is already cut lifts and enters again. The fig8 path has about 93 lateral rapids. The Auto order has 18.\n\nResults of this:\n- The cycle time is longer.\n- One generation of the fig8 Outside path with its verifier takes about 170 s in debug (15 s in release). The two fig8 Outside tests are in the heavy lane for that reason.\n\nNecessary work:\n1. Measure: the count of lifts for each level, and the reason for each one (no cut material near the join, a wall between the pieces, the 0.9 tool radius rule).\n2. Order the pieces of a ring so that more joins stay down (for example, follow one side of the part before the other side), without a cut at the full tool width and without a link through stock that is not cut.\n3. Find why the verifier is slow on this path, and make the two fig8 tests fast enough for the default tier, or add a light twin.\n\nRefs #3316\n",
